---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Flow from "../components/Flow.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Han Che">
  <section class="wrap page-heading">
    <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
    <h1>
      A habit of
      <br />
      looking closer.
    </h1>
    <p class="page-deck">
      I’m Han Che, an undergraduate in Data Science and Big Data Technology at
      Xi’an Jiaotong-Liverpool University.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap about-grid">
    <Flow />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Questions, code, context.</h2>
      <p>
        I’m interested in machine learning, data science, reproducible research,
        research software engineering and computational methods. My public work
        includes atmospheric data pipelines, ozone prediction, language-model
        tool selection and relational database design.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the path to a result: source records, evaluation choices,
        and the assumptions that remain after the code runs. I want the software
        to make those decisions easier to inspect.
      </p>
      <h2>Technical practice</h2>
      <p>
        Python, SQL/PostgreSQL, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, PyTorch and Git
        feature in my public projects. The research pages link to code and
        documented limitations so the evidence can speak for itself.
      </p>
      <h2>Ways of seeing</h2>
      <p>
        Photography and visual storytelling are personal interests. This site
        makes space for that work without substituting stock imagery or invented
        photographs.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/photography/">
        Visit the photography space ↗
      </a>
      <h2>What I’m curious about</h2>
      <p>
        How can environmental models remain useful outside their fitting
        conditions? What does reproducibility require when the original data
        cannot be redistributed? How can a visual explanation make an
        uncertainty easier to understand?
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">
        Start a conversation ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
